<page title="Notes — Blog" description="Writing about tools, craft and small bets" theme="paper" favicon="/logo.svg">
<style>
.feat{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr;gap:1.5rem;align-items:center;margin-bottom:2.5rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden;background:var(--surface)}
.feat img{width:100%;height:100%;min-height:220px;object-fit:cover}
.feat .txt{padding:1.5rem}
.post img{width:100%;aspect-ratio:16/9;object-fit:cover;border-radius:calc(var(--radius) - 4px);margin-bottom:.85rem}
.bar{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.6rem;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:.75rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:1rem;font-size:.88rem}
@media(max-width:800px){.feat{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
<navbar brand="Notes" icon="book-open" links="Latest:#latest, Archive:#archive" cta="Subscribe:#subscribe">
  <themeswitch />
</navbar>
<div class="bar">
  <span class="muted">Template · Blog</span>
  <div class="stk-row">
    <button size="sm" variant="secondary" href="/templates" icon="arrow-left">Gallery</button>
    <button size="sm" variant="secondary" icon="copy" data-copy="stk new my-site --template blog">Copy CLI</button>
  </div>
</div>
<hero>
  <badge icon="sparkles">New issue</badge>
  <h1>Writing about tools, craft and small bets</h1>
  <p class="lead">Short essays. No growth hacks.</p>
</hero>
<section id="latest">
  <div class="feat">
    <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1499750310107-5fef28a66643?w=900&amp;q=80" alt="Featured" />
    <div class="txt">
      <badge>Featured</badge>
      <h2 style="font-size:1.6rem;margin:.4rem 0">Why one-file sites still win</h2>
      <p class="muted">A case for keeping surface area tiny when you just need a page.</p>
      <button href="#" size="sm" variant="secondary">Read article</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <h2>Latest</h2>
  <grid cols="3">
    <div class="post">
      <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1516321318423-f06f85e504b3?w=600&amp;q=80" alt="" loading="lazy" />
      <h3>Theme systems without a design system</h3>
      <p class="muted">CSS variables, restraint, and ten good defaults.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="post">
      <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1461749280684-dccba630e2f6?w=600&amp;q=80" alt="" loading="lazy" />
      <h3>Shipping static in 2026</h3>
      <p class="muted">What still matters when everything can be a framework.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="post">
      <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1486312338219-ce68d2c6f44d?w=600&amp;q=80" alt="" loading="lazy" />
      <h3>Delete more</h3>
      <p class="muted">Why removing features can increase retention.</p>
    </div>
  </grid>
</section>
<section id="archive">
  <h2>Archive</h2>
  <md>
- **Mar 2026** — Why one-file sites still win
- **Feb 2026** — Theme systems without a design system
- **Jan 2026** — Shipping static in 2026
  </md>
</section>
<section id="subscribe">
  <h2>Subscribe</h2>
  <alert type="success">No spam. One note when something is worth sending.</alert>
</section>
<footer>© Notes. Built with Stack.</footer>
</page>
